    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d125">

                <pb facs="0177" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg85"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins
                    Papers: Telegram (paraphrase)</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Presidents Special
                        Assistant</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d125-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-13">13 November 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>(Personal and secret for Hopkins from
                        Harriman)</p>
                <p>Have had no reply to those portions of my 092359<anchor n="2" xml:id="d125-f2"/>
                    and 120001<anchor n="3" xml:id="d125-f3"/> regarding Molotov’s desire for information about Cairo Conference. I hope
                    this information can be supplied soonest possible even if only in a preliminary
                        way.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d125-f4"/> …</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d125-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d125-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the United States Naval Attaché, Moscow, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d125-f2" n="2" xml:id="d125-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram of November 9, 1943, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg76">p. 76</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d125-f3" n="3" xml:id="d125-f3-content">
                <p>Telegram of November 12, 1943, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg80">p. 80</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d125-f4" n="4" xml:id="d125-f4-content">
                <p>See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg81">p. 81</ref>, footnote
                    4. For the portion of this message omitted at this point, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg189">p. 189</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
